  "name": "Detect scope creep in client emails against your SOW with Gmail, OpenAI and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0a856af8-2243-48df-913c-0f03fa38e572",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1100,
        "content": "## Detect scope creep in client emails against your SOW with Gmail, OpenAI and Google Sheets\n\n**Who's it for**\nAgencies, consultants and freelancers who lose margin to scope creep. \"Can you just quickly add...\" emails get done for free because nobody checks them against the contract.\n\n**How it works**\n1. A Gmail trigger watches your inbox. Emails from client domains you've mapped to a statement of work (SOW) are picked up; everything else is ignored.\n2. The client's SOW is read live from Google Docs, so contract edits apply instantly.\n3. OpenAI compares the request with the SOW. It returns a verdict (**in scope**, **out of scope** or **unclear**), the clause it relied on, an effort estimate in hours and a polite change-order reply. Emails that aren't requests are dropped.\n4. Every request is logged to a **Scope Log** sheet with its verdict, estimated hours and value at your rate. That gives you a running ledger of unbilled work per client for renewal and upsell conversations.\n5. For out-of-scope or unclear requests, your team gets a Slack alert. The change-order reply is saved as a **Gmail draft** in the same thread. Nothing is sent without you.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Create a Google Sheet tab named `Scope Log` with these headers: checked_at, client_domain, from_email, subject, request_summary, verdict, matching_clause, estimated_hours, estimated_value, thread_link.\n2. In **Configure settings**, map each client email domain to its SOW Google Doc URL in `client_sow_map`. Add the Sheet ID, hourly rate, currency, Slack channel and sign-off name.\n3. Connect Gmail (trigger and draft node), Google Docs, Google Sheets, OpenAI and Slack credentials, then activate.\n\n**Requirements**\nGmail, Google Docs (one doc per client SOW), Google Sheets, an OpenAI API key and Slack.\n\n**How to customize**\n- Tune the reply tone in the AI prompt.\n- Change the trigger's Gmail search to watch a shared client inbox.\n- Add a monthly summary that totals estimated_value per client from the Scope Log."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
